# Test-only packages CI installs beside the engine (never shipped, never in
# the engine the setup scripts make). This is the source:
# requirements-ci.txt is generated from it, exact versions and SHA-256
# hashes, resolved together with requirements-gis.txt and requirements-db.txt
# so they install side by side. Edit this file, then run
#   python packaging/engine/compile-requirements.py
#
# - playwright: drives the companion window in a browser (app/ui/e2e).
# - selenium: drives the desktop app through WebDriver (app/desktop/e2e).
# - pyyaml: reads the settings files those scripts check.
# (psycopg, for PostGIS, comes from requirements-db.txt.)
